&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 13.8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1) Settlements of these amounts are made within equity and are considered non-cash financing activities.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Affiliate Balances and Activities&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;We participate in KMI's cash management program, which matches the short-term cash surpluses and needs of participating affiliates, thus minimizing total borrowings from outside sources. KMI uses the cash management program to settle intercompany transactions between participating affiliates. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, we had a note receivable from KMI of approximately $548.5 million and $605.6 million, respectively. The interest rate on this note is variable and was 3.9% and 4.7% as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. These amounts are included in Account 123 "Investments in Associated Companies" on our balance sheets. For the twelve months ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded interest income of $27.7 million and $35.5 million, respectively, related to our participation in the cash management program.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
