&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 13.8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;(1) Assets recoverable without earning a return.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Our significant regulatory assets and liabilities include:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Taxes on capitalized funds used during construction. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;Amounts represent the deferred income taxes on AFUDC equity funds. These amounts are recoverable in our tariff rates over the depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Dredging costs. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;We have a FERC approved tariff mechanism to track the dredging costs incurred at our facility. An annual filing is made to update the dredging surcharge. Our tariff provides that the difference between the amount of revenue received from the dredging surcharge and the amount of dredging costs incurred over the applicable annual period will be flowed through or charged to shippers by including such difference in the calculation to update the dredging surcharge in the annual filing.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded a net regulatory expense of $0.2 million and a net regulatory benefit of $1.6 million, respectively, related to the provisions of this tracker.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Income tax related.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt; Amounts represent the anticipated return to ratepayers of deferred income taxes, primarily as a result of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017, which lowered the U.S. federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% effective January 1, 2018. These amounts are amortized to Account 411.1 &amp;#8220;Provision for Deferred Income Taxes &amp;#8211; Credit&amp;#8221; over the remaining depreciable lives of the assets to which they apply.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;Electric power costs. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;We have FERC approved tariff mechanisms to track the electricity costs incurred at our facility, including costs incurred by the K-6 compressor, K-7 compressor and ship loading service. An annual filing is made to update each of the electric power cost rates. Our tariff provides that the difference between the amount of revenue received from the electric power cost rates and the amount of electric costs incurred over the applicable annual period will be flowed through or charged to shippers by including such difference in the calculation to update the electric power cost rates in the annual filings.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;For each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recorded a net regulatory benefit of $1.0 million related to the provisions of these electric power cost trackers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7. Contract Prepayment&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;During 2023, we entered into an agreement whereby Shell prepaid certain fixed reservation charges under its long-term shiploading contract. The prepayment is being recognized as revenue over the original contract term ending in 2035. During the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we recognized approximately $55.9 million and $56.1 million, respectively, of revenue related to this prepayment. Unamortized balances as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 of $531.1 million and $587.0 million, respectively, are included in Account 253 &amp;#8220;Other Deferred Credits&amp;#8221; on our balance sheets.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8. Recent Accounting Pronouncement&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic;"&gt;ASU No. 2025-06&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 18.4pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 16pt; -aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt; background-color: #ffffff;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On September 18, 2025, the Financial Accounting Standards Board issued ASU No. 2025-06, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#8220;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Intangibles&amp;#8212;Goodwill and Other&amp;#8212;Internal-Use Software (Subtopic 350-40): Targeted Improvements to the Accounting for Internal-Use Software.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#8221; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;This ASU modernizes the accounting guidance for the costs to develop software for internal use by removing outdated stage-based cost capitalization rules and replacing them with a probability-based cost-capitalization framework that aligns better with current software development methods. This ASU will be effective for annual periods beginning after December 15, 2027, for interim reporting periods beginning within those annual periods, and early adoption is permitted. Management is currently evaluating this ASU to determine its impact on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="Tag1386" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; color: black;"&gt;1. None&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
